# PayslipMax — 7-Tier Parsing Architecture & Offline Gemma Roadmap

This document outlines the architecture, readiness status, and multi-sprint execution plan for upgrading PayslipMax to a **7-Tier High-Precision Parsing Architecture** featuring offline Gemma fallback for ambiguous tokens.

---

## 1. 7-Tier Architecture Overview

The parsing pipeline processes monthly PCDA(O) military payslips through seven sequential stages, guaranteeing deterministic mathematical accuracy while leveraging on-device LLM intelligence only when spatial rules encounter ambiguity.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    T1[Tier 1: PDF Native Parser\nPDFKit / PDFBox] --> T2[Tier 2: Coordinate & Font Aware Parser\nx, y, w, h, fontSize, isBold]
    T2 --> T3[Tier 3: Table Reconstruction\nGridReconstructor & RowPairing]
    T3 --> T4[Tier 4: Field Detector\nTokenTableClassifier & PayslipPatternConfig]
    T4 --> T5[Tier 5: Confidence Engine\nReconciliationSolver & REVIEW_THRESHOLD]
    T5 -->|Low Confidence / Unmatched Tokens| T6[Tier 6: Offline Gemma Fallback\nLocalGemmaProvider AI Parsing]
    T5 -->|High Confidence| T7[Tier 7: Schema Validator\nMathematical Invariants Check]
    T6 --> T7
    T7 --> Store[(Encrypted Room DB\nStructured ParsedPayslip JSON)]
```

